{"uid":"estorides_core/osiris_sources.py","name":"osiris_sources.py","qualname":"estorides_core/osiris_sources.py","kind":"module","file":"estorides_core/osiris_sources.py","line":1,"end_line":525,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"estorides_core.osiris_sources ============================= Extra OSINT endpoints borrowed from the Osiris project (simplifaisoul/osiris).","description":"Each function returns a Flask Response-ready dict; the Blueprint in `estorides_web` wires them up to public routes.\n\nWhy a separate module:\n  The main 99 sources are YAML-defined and go through the orchestrator\n  pipeline (parser → entity extraction → KG). The Osiris-style\n  endpoints are narrower: they hit a single free API and return a\n  flat JSON response without going through the orchestrator. Mixing\n  them into the YAML registry would force a parallel \"raw passthrough\"\n  parser and bloat `parsers.py`. Keeping them here makes the boundary\n  explicit and easy to audit.\n\nSource map (Osiris → here):\n  /api/osiris/bgp        bgpview.io (keyless)\n  /api/osiris/mac        macvendors.co (keyless)\n  /api/osiris/phone      local libphonenumber + region centroid table\n  /api/osiris/github     api.github.com (keyless, rate-limited)\n  /api/osiris/leaks      api.xposedornot.com (keyless, more detail than HIBP)\n  /api/osiris/cisa-kev   cisa.gov KEV JSON feed\n  /api/osiris/malware    feodotracker.abuse.ch + urlhaus-api.abuse.ch","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["estorides_core/osiris_sources.py::COUNTRY_CENTROIDS","estorides_core/osiris_sources.py::CACHE_DIR","estorides_core/osiris_sources.py::fetch_bgp","estorides_core/osiris_sources.py::fetch_mac","estorides_core/osiris_sources.py::fetch_phone","estorides_core/osiris_sources.py::fetch_github_user","estorides_core/osiris_sources.py::fetch_leaks","estorides_core/osiris_sources.py::fetch_cisa_kev","estorides_core/osiris_sources.py::fetch_malware_c2"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
